# The Options block of a page ends with a row `Print help` spelled as the
# requests for help laws/HelpWordAsksForHelp.bend answers on its command: `-h, --help` when
# the command has neither the short spelling `h` nor the long spelling `help`,
# `--help` when it has `h` but not `help`, and no row when it has `help`. On
# the root page of a spec with a version a row `Print version` follows,
# spelled as the requests laws/VersionWordAsksForVersion.bend answers: `-V, --version` when the root
# has neither the short spelling `V` nor the long spelling `version`,
# `--version` when it has `V` but not `version`, and no row when it has
# `version`. These rows are laid out as the other rows of the block, and make
# the usage line show `[OPTIONS]`.
#
# also rests on: laws/BuiltinsListed.bend
import Base


